  "verbalization": "Epi-Fibrauretinoside A is shown to have a target relationship with SMMC-7721 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link involving Valacyclovir hydrolase. This enzyme is a target of the compound and is ultimately linked to SMMC-7721, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a key metabolic pathway. The second pathway connects Epi-Fibrauretinoside A to a dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase, which is targeted by Javanicoside F and ultimately affects SMMC-7721. The third pathway also links Epi-Fibrauretinoside A to a similar kinase, which is targeted by a different compound and leads to SMMC-7721. These findings suggest that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A may exert its effects through the modulation of protein kinases, potentially influencing cellular processes in SMMC-7721 cells. The evidence supports a mechanism involving kinase inhibition, but the exact nature of the kinase and its role in SMMC-7721 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism and its relevance to the disease state.",
